Astra’s review found three reproducible correctness issues on `f7c86349`. I would request changes.

::code-comment{title="[P2] Match the function declarator, not arbitrary signature text" body="A free function `int Add(decltype(&acct::Ledger::Add) member)` passes this owner check because its parameter mentions the member. A full graph reproduction redirects `ledger.Add(3)` to that unrelated free function with type_inferred resolution. Match the candidate's actual function declarator and lexical owner instead of searching its entire signature." file="/Users/thomi/.codex/worktrees/c68d/entire-graph/internal/sem/provider.go" start=9100 end=9104 priority=2}

::code-comment{title="[P2] Account for the definition's enclosing namespace" body="For `namespace acct { int Ledger::Add(int amount) { ... } }`, the candidate signature is `int Ledger::Add(int amount)`, while the declaration owner is acct::Ledger. This check rejects the valid definition. A full graph reproduction leaves the caller pointing at the header declaration, so the implementation loses its callers and impact information. Preserve and compare the definition's lexical namespace context." file="/Users/thomi/.codex/worktrees/c68d/entire-graph/internal/sem/provider.go" start=9101 end=9107 priority=2}

::code-comment{title="[P2] Preserve shared declaration specifiers" body="Reconstructing a signature from only typeText and the declarator drops shared specifiers such as virtual, static, and constexpr. Changing `int f(), g();` to `virtual int f(), g();` produces identical method signatures, fingerprints, and body hashes in a parser reproduction, hiding the API change. Include the shared declaration specifiers while excluding sibling declarators." file="/Users/thomi/.codex/worktrees/c68d/entire-graph/internal/sem/parser.go" start=5050 end=5055 priority=2}

Existing C++ tests pass; the new reproductions fail as described. Temporary test code was removed and the worktree is clean. The trail’s recorded approval has not been changed.

